WEBVTT

00:29.930 --> 00:31.920
<b>Ton</b>-chan the Glutton

00:31.920 --> 00:33.300
<b>Ton</b>-chan the Glutton

01:09.970 --> 01:11.970
<b>Ren-nii?!</b>

01:09.970 --> 01:11.970
<b>Ren-nii?!</b>

01:10.210 --> 01:11.480
<i>Ren-nii?!</i>

01:16.560 --> 01:21.350
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

01:16.560 --> 01:21.350
<b>Mysterious Disappearances</b>

02:42.020 --> 02:46.020
<b>Mysterious Disappearances
Ogawa Sumireko</b>

02:43.170 --> 02:46.020
<i>I'm Ogawa Sumireko.</i>

02:43.640 --> 02:49.650
<b>A Ticket, a Video, and Mysterious Disappearances</b>

02:43.640 --> 02:49.650
<b>A Ticket, a Video, and Mysterious Disappearances</b>

02:46.020 --> 02:49.650
<i>I have a friend who's never at a loss 
for something to say: Adashino Ren.</i>

02:49.650 --> 02:52.710
<i>This is but a humble account 
of our friendship and parting.</i>

02:54.510 --> 02:56.660
He still hasn't read it.

02:56.660 --> 02:58.570
What's the deal?

03:00.660 --> 03:05.660
<i>The device you are trying to reach is 
either outside the service area or—</i>

03:17.270 --> 03:19.060
Good morning.

03:19.060 --> 03:20.680
Good morning, Oto-san!

03:26.350 --> 03:30.690
Uname-sensei, I'm sorry to make 
you look after me like this again.

03:30.990 --> 03:35.690
It's perfectly all right! It's summer 
vacation, so I have the day off, too.

03:36.090 --> 03:40.200
You said you wanted ramen for breakfast, so...

03:40.200 --> 03:41.960
I went all-out!

03:53.200 --> 03:57.790
<i>The device you are trying to reach is either 
outside the service area or turned off.</i>

03:58.690 --> 04:00.840
Don't tell me he blocked me...

04:05.140 --> 04:06.850
Thank you for the meal.

04:07.170 --> 04:08.530
Was it tasty?

04:08.530 --> 04:12.200
Yes! I've never had such 
extravagant ramen before.

04:12.200 --> 04:13.860
I'm so glad!

04:13.860 --> 04:16.860
You can come over again 
any time you want, okay?

04:16.860 --> 04:19.250
Thank you.

04:20.830 --> 04:21.870
So...

04:24.430 --> 04:28.480
I have a favor to ask.

04:30.220 --> 04:31.670
What is it?

04:49.010 --> 04:50.140
Sensei...

04:51.680 --> 04:53.650
Thank you for doing this.

04:54.570 --> 04:57.900
Yes, of course. Just leave it to me!

05:00.230 --> 05:02.410
Well, if you'll excuse me.

05:03.280 --> 05:04.910
Safe travels!

05:06.860 --> 05:07.910
Sensei...

05:09.200 --> 05:11.240
Thank you so much.

05:18.240 --> 05:19.610
Take care of yourself.

05:26.930 --> 05:31.350
<b>KISARAGI</b>

05:48.360 --> 05:49.370
Hey!

05:50.700 --> 05:53.210
O-Old man?

05:53.810 --> 05:55.100
Why are you here?

05:55.720 --> 05:58.710
Normally, I'd never come 
to a place like this.

05:59.230 --> 06:01.720
There's been a cat prowling 
around here lately, right?

06:02.020 --> 06:06.200
But I know how complicated your situation is, 
so I came with a little advice.

06:06.200 --> 06:07.150
Advice?

06:07.150 --> 06:08.970
You're leaving tomorrow, right?

06:08.970 --> 06:13.520
What if I am? And what do you mean, 
my situation is complicated?

06:13.520 --> 06:15.210
Do you really want me to say it?

06:15.210 --> 06:16.730
S-Say what?

06:17.400 --> 06:21.490
You have no intention of going back 
with your little sister, do you?

06:22.850 --> 06:23.990
Uh-oh.

06:23.990 --> 06:25.940
<b>KISARAGI</b>

06:24.310 --> 06:26.620
The cat'll be here soon.

06:38.640 --> 06:41.120
<i>Ren-nii, did something happen?</i>

06:41.120 --> 06:44.510
<i>Oto, there's something 
I want to talk to you about.</i>

06:46.770 --> 06:51.160
Tomorrow, we'll be going back 
on the evening train.

06:51.730 --> 06:52.520
Yeah...

06:52.520 --> 06:57.270
And you'll be going on the 
first train by yourself.

06:57.270 --> 07:00.770
By myself? Why?

07:01.270 --> 07:04.280
There are still some things I have left to do.

07:04.270 --> 07:06.280
<b>K</b>

07:04.270 --> 07:06.280
<b>I</b>

07:04.270 --> 07:06.280
<b>S</b>

07:04.270 --> 07:06.280
<b>A</b>

07:04.270 --> 07:06.280
<b>R</b>

07:04.270 --> 07:06.280
<b>A</b>

07:04.270 --> 07:06.280
<b>G</b>

07:04.270 --> 07:06.280
<b>I</b>

07:05.090 --> 07:07.450
I'll come after you on the next train.

07:08.280 --> 07:11.960
Then I'll go on that train with you!

07:11.960 --> 07:14.660
We can't, because of the way 
the ticketing worked out.

07:15.130 --> 07:19.790
So you'll go first, 
and I'll be right after you.

07:26.510 --> 07:29.300
Is it okay if I sleep over 
somewhere tonight, too?

07:29.760 --> 07:31.220
When will you be back?

07:31.220 --> 07:32.920
Tomorrow morning.

07:32.920 --> 07:34.700
Make sure you come back safely.

07:48.420 --> 07:49.500
Who are you?

07:52.750 --> 07:54.580
Are you the little sister, meow?

07:54.580 --> 07:55.990
What do you want?

07:55.990 --> 07:59.580
They say you're Mysterious 
Disappearances' little sister.

07:59.580 --> 08:00.730
Is that true?

08:00.730 --> 08:01.570
What?

08:01.570 --> 08:04.590
Did you really believe that?

08:08.740 --> 08:11.720
You're the one getting in 
Ren-nii's way, aren't you?

08:11.720 --> 08:13.670
Hiss!

08:15.340 --> 08:19.230
Maybe I'll have you die 
along with your Ren-nii.

08:19.730 --> 08:20.730
Stop it.

08:20.730 --> 08:21.850
Huh?

08:22.230 --> 08:26.530
You have no business with Oto. 
Don't you lay a finger on her.

08:26.530 --> 08:32.510
I told you, didn't I? I can't have you 
going around getting rid of Curiosities.

08:32.510 --> 08:36.620
Then there's no problem. 
Oto and I will both be gone soon.

08:36.930 --> 08:39.020
I won't get in your way anymore.

08:39.020 --> 08:40.550
Are you being serious?

08:40.550 --> 08:42.060
I am.

08:43.480 --> 08:45.130
That blasted kid!

08:45.490 --> 08:49.130
What happened to that promise 
to read my new novel?

08:49.620 --> 08:53.640
Then does that mean you'll 
never appear before me again?

08:53.640 --> 08:55.410
That's what it means.

08:53.640 --> 09:05.650
<b>KISARAGI</b>

08:57.660 --> 09:00.420
If that's true, then it's very good news!

09:00.420 --> 09:03.500
But how are you going to prove it to me?

09:03.500 --> 09:05.630
We're taking this evening's train.

09:06.080 --> 09:07.650
And then we'll be gone.

09:08.550 --> 09:11.790
You'll be able to sense that, won't you?

09:12.420 --> 09:13.660
I see.

09:13.660 --> 09:17.050
Then I'll hold off on 
killing you here and now.

09:17.050 --> 09:19.560
In exchange, you'd better 
not be lying to me.

09:19.560 --> 09:21.670
If I'm lying, it's only about one thing.

09:21.670 --> 09:22.760
Meow?

09:23.670 --> 09:27.130
In any case, I won't be here anymore 
after today. That is the truth.

09:23.670 --> 09:28.170
<b>KISARAGI</b>

09:27.130 --> 09:28.170
Don't worry.

09:29.110 --> 09:31.170
It seems you've escaped death for now.

09:31.170 --> 09:33.400
Everyone! We're leaving.

09:42.010 --> 09:46.190
The new moon sits in the heart of blackness, 
being stained darker and darker.

09:46.770 --> 09:51.190
The arrow of the crescent moon shoots 
to the east, racing faster and faster.

09:51.660 --> 09:55.900
The half moon sinks, and for a moment, 
it touches, growing rounder and rounder.

09:56.260 --> 10:00.350
Chasing the shadow of the night of the 
full moon, around and around they go.

10:14.970 --> 10:16.970
<b>Apartment Wife</b>

10:14.970 --> 10:16.970
<b>Apartment Wife</b>

10:16.970 --> 10:19.470
<b>KISARAGI</b>

10:17.780 --> 10:19.470
Now, let's head back.

10:19.470 --> 10:21.980
<b>KISARAGI</b>

10:35.820 --> 10:36.990
Oto.

10:36.990 --> 10:40.490
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

10:36.990 --> 10:40.490
<b><u>KISARAGI
</u>Ticket</b>

10:36.990 --> 10:40.490
<b>12-3-45</b>

10:37.500 --> 10:39.670
It's almost time to go.

10:41.800 --> 10:43.210
Let's head to the platform.

10:44.000 --> 10:47.570
From now on, the two of us 
are going to live happy lives.

10:52.760 --> 10:54.260
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

10:52.760 --> 10:54.260
<b><u>KISARAGI
</u>Ticket</b>

10:52.760 --> 10:54.260
<b>12-3-45</b>

10:55.160 --> 10:58.320
All right, Oto. 
I'll be coming right after you.

10:58.320 --> 10:59.760
Just wait for me.

11:03.290 --> 11:04.270
I...

11:05.120 --> 11:10.590
I've lived the last ten years believing 
I was really your little sister.

11:11.490 --> 11:12.380
Yeah.

11:12.780 --> 11:15.040
But earlier, I remembered.

11:15.350 --> 11:17.930
Something had appeared before me,

11:17.930 --> 11:21.240
and I was certain that my big brother 
had caught up to me,

11:21.240 --> 11:23.200
so I called out, "Ren-nii!"

11:23.200 --> 11:24.820
But I was wrong.

11:25.230 --> 11:26.040
Really?

11:26.040 --> 11:29.600
Back then, I called you Ren-nii...

11:30.540 --> 11:34.600
so you turned into a Curiosity 
called Adashino Ren, didn't you?

11:35.830 --> 11:37.560
That might be true.

11:38.790 --> 11:43.260
And that's why I can place a curse on you.

11:43.850 --> 11:45.430
What do you mean?

11:45.430 --> 11:53.240
If you can't be there to see me living 
happily, you won't be able to bear it.

11:53.240 --> 11:57.680
That's why we have to see each other again.

11:57.680 --> 11:59.040
That's the curse.

11:59.460 --> 12:02.460
Of course. And we'll be seeing 
each other again very soon.

12:03.450 --> 12:07.960
And that was your one and only lie, wasn't it?

12:07.960 --> 12:10.460
<b>The train is approaching
The train is approaching</b>

12:07.960 --> 12:12.960
<i>For... safety, please... behind... line.</i>

12:15.960 --> 12:19.150
Ren-nii, thank you for everything.

12:28.980 --> 12:30.600
I won't forget you.

12:47.540 --> 12:50.040
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

12:47.540 --> 12:50.040
<b><u>KISARAGI
</u>Ticket</b>

12:47.540 --> 12:50.040
<b>12-3-45</b>

12:53.440 --> 12:56.500
He really did disappear.

12:57.590 --> 13:01.700
Chasing the shadow of the night of the 
full moon, around and around they go.

13:03.520 --> 13:04.680
Well, now.

13:05.020 --> 13:06.680
What's all this?

13:09.820 --> 13:14.670
You don't see many Bearers of Youth around. 
Are you the one Adashino-kun talked about?

13:14.670 --> 13:15.440
Huh?

13:19.040 --> 13:23.820
Apparently, Adashino-kun's one regret is 
that he never got to take a bath with you.

13:25.300 --> 13:27.330
Old man, how do you know about...

13:27.330 --> 13:29.980
The train's already left the station.

13:30.600 --> 13:33.140
But the little sister 
was the only one on board.

13:33.140 --> 13:35.840
What? Then where's Adashino-kun?

13:35.840 --> 13:41.090
Did you know that Adashino-kun and 
his little sister weren't actually siblings?

13:41.090 --> 13:45.100
No. But what does that mean?

13:45.100 --> 13:47.990
He finally confessed everything to me.

13:48.660 --> 13:53.100
He said that Oto's brother, 
the real Ren-nii, is over there.

13:53.100 --> 13:55.920
The "real Ren-nii"?

13:57.380 --> 13:59.610
Do you want to know my name?

13:59.610 --> 14:02.110
I don't think I ever asked.

14:02.530 --> 14:07.120
People call me the Old Man of Time and Space.

14:07.120 --> 14:10.590
I'm sure we'll be seeing each other again.

14:15.630 --> 14:18.700
<i>Please let me read a new work of yours.</i>

14:19.290 --> 14:21.130
<i>I am your fan.</i>

14:21.410 --> 14:26.390
You'd better take responsibility for this 
and make sure to read my new work.

14:26.390 --> 14:28.020
<i>I promise I will.</i>

14:33.560 --> 14:36.060
<b>Mysterious Disappearances
Ogawa Sumireko</b>

14:47.500 --> 14:48.890
Coming.

14:49.520 --> 14:52.790
Good morning! It's Uname!

14:52.790 --> 14:54.710
Huh? Uname-sensei?

14:55.150 --> 15:00.210
I'm so sorry. I never asked for your email, 
so I've just turned up out of the blue!

15:00.530 --> 15:02.910
I have some urgent business, you see.

15:04.190 --> 15:08.410
I'm impressed! This is exactly 
how I'd picture a novelist's home!

15:08.410 --> 15:11.220
I'm sorry. This is all I have right now.

15:11.860 --> 15:14.560
I'm on summer vacation right now, 
so it's totally okay!

15:14.560 --> 15:17.230
Oh, my! Is this the novel you talked about?

15:15.260 --> 15:17.230
<b>Mysterious Disappearances
Ogawa Sumireko</b>

15:17.630 --> 15:19.470
You've finished it?

15:19.470 --> 15:21.730
Then you've turned your dream into reality.

15:21.730 --> 15:24.000
No, it isn't quite done.

15:24.000 --> 15:26.540
But more importantly, 
what was your urgent business?

15:26.540 --> 15:27.740
Oh, right.

15:28.210 --> 15:29.240
Here.

15:29.240 --> 15:31.290
That's Oto-chan's.

15:31.290 --> 15:33.600
She stopped by the day before yesterday.

15:33.600 --> 15:36.000
She had me take a video for her,

15:36.300 --> 15:40.760
and she begged me not to 
let you see it before today.

15:41.380 --> 15:43.160
A video of Oto-chan?

15:43.160 --> 15:44.510
That's right.

15:44.510 --> 15:46.010
Will you watch it now?

15:46.010 --> 15:47.510
Of course.

15:55.230 --> 16:00.630
<i>Um, apartment wife... 
I'm going away without seeing you first.</i>

16:01.000 --> 16:02.370
<i>I'm sorry for that.</i>

16:03.440 --> 16:08.250
<i>We went to school together, 
and to the bathhouse.</i>

16:08.760 --> 16:12.460
<i>And you let me sleep over.</i>

16:12.930 --> 16:16.000
<i>You worked so hard with me 
to help Shizuku-san.</i>

16:16.350 --> 16:20.090
<i>And you treated me to ramen. It was so good.</i>

16:21.010 --> 16:24.390
<i>You saved Nodoka for me, too.</i>

16:25.560 --> 16:29.720
<i>I never once said thank you, so...</i>

16:30.510 --> 16:33.710
<i>So I'll say it now, okay?</i>

16:38.150 --> 16:42.150
<i>Thank you, Sumireko-san...</i>

16:44.550 --> 16:45.890
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

16:47.400 --> 16:49.080
<i>Sumireko-san!</i>

17:02.310 --> 17:04.590
Oto-san told me something.

17:04.880 --> 17:08.880
She said it was because she met you

17:08.880 --> 17:13.600
that this world became so very, very fun!

17:12.090 --> 17:13.600
<b>KISARAGI</b>

17:26.220 --> 17:28.610
I'm certain it was somewhere around here.

17:49.630 --> 17:51.630
<b>Gyokushin-dou Bookstore</b>

17:55.140 --> 17:58.140
Well, now, young lady. 
It's been a while, hasn't it?

17:59.650 --> 18:01.140
How many years has it been?

18:01.520 --> 18:03.670
I apologize for my long absence.

18:04.190 --> 18:05.150
I, um...

18:06.000 --> 18:08.400
I brought this as thanks.

18:08.730 --> 18:11.010
It's a new novel of mine.

18:11.650 --> 18:16.910
<b>Mysterious Disappearances
Ogawa Sumireko</b>

18:12.210 --> 18:13.530
I hope you'll accept this offering.

18:13.530 --> 18:16.910
My, it's been a long time 
since I've had a new book.

18:19.710 --> 18:23.580
I'll read it right away. Why don't 
you have a look around the shop?

18:23.580 --> 18:24.560
I will.

18:32.550 --> 18:34.550
<b>The Price of Adultery</b>

18:37.050 --> 18:39.070
"'Of course I don't love her.'

18:39.070 --> 18:43.090
In that moment, Julia looked 
behind me and smiled, just a little.

18:43.090 --> 18:47.060
When I turned around, 
I realized that it was all over.

18:47.060 --> 18:49.100
The person standing there was my wife.

18:49.100 --> 18:53.070
And from behind the frozen mask 
of her expression, she said,

18:53.070 --> 18:54.940
'I hope you'll be very happy.'"

18:55.820 --> 18:58.030
I've finally found it.

18:58.540 --> 18:59.840
Young lady?

19:00.370 --> 19:01.510
Yes?

19:02.630 --> 19:06.260
Say, why does this "Mysterious 
Disappearances" fellow in the story

19:06.260 --> 19:12.400
never end up reading the heroine's 
completed new novel?

19:12.400 --> 19:13.840
Well...

19:14.160 --> 19:16.450
I don't know the answer myself.

19:18.420 --> 19:22.600
You're the one who wrote it, 
but you don't know?

19:22.600 --> 19:24.540
That's right. I'm sorry.

19:24.540 --> 19:25.910
I have a thought.

19:25.910 --> 19:26.660
Huh?

19:26.660 --> 19:28.220
This Mysterious Disappearances...

19:28.220 --> 19:31.350
He never read the new novel 
that he'd promised to.

19:31.350 --> 19:34.610
In short, he's deliberately giving 
himself regrets tied to this world.

19:34.910 --> 19:38.620
In leaving these regrets, 
he's trying to hold himself here.

19:38.880 --> 19:42.800
That's how much he must love 
something here in this world.

19:42.800 --> 19:45.550
How do you know that?

19:45.550 --> 19:50.510
After reading tens of thousands of books, 
you start to understand a little.

19:51.240 --> 19:54.280
I'll rewrite that part!

19:54.280 --> 19:55.880
You mustn't.

19:55.880 --> 20:00.050
Within the confines of this novel, 
the heroine doesn't know that.

20:00.050 --> 20:01.890
That's why it works.

20:02.190 --> 20:05.890
If you rewrite it, Mysterious Disappearances' 
feelings will come to an end.

20:05.890 --> 20:08.390
His feelings will end?

20:08.390 --> 20:11.390
<b>Mysterious Disappearances
Ogawa Sumireko</b>

20:08.390 --> 20:11.400
Now, I'm going to read this one more time.

20:11.730 --> 20:13.900
I'm sorry, but could you wait 
just a little longer?

20:39.930 --> 20:41.800
Adashino-kun?

20:42.130 --> 20:44.810
If you're Adashino-kun, then please listen!

20:44.810 --> 20:47.650
The truth is, there's something I haven't said.

20:47.650 --> 20:50.810
It seems I'm no good without you around.

20:51.260 --> 20:53.480
I don't feel like writing anything.

20:53.850 --> 20:56.410
You have to teach me all those new things!

20:56.820 --> 20:59.570
Which means... Which means...

20:59.570 --> 21:01.650
I need you!

21:06.080 --> 21:07.820
Adashino-kun...

21:08.440 --> 21:11.000
I need you.

21:12.340 --> 21:14.300
I'm not taking a bath with you, though.

21:14.300 --> 21:16.000
What?!

22:46.050 --> 22:50.060
Adashino-kun, it's been a real lifesaver 
having you back at work.

22:50.060 --> 22:53.560
<b>Midori Bookstore</b>

22:50.560 --> 22:53.560
It's so hard to find part-timers nowadays.

22:53.560 --> 22:56.950
We had a rough time of it 
while you were gone, you know.

22:53.560 --> 22:58.560
<b>This Month's New Titles</b>

22:53.560 --> 22:58.560
<b>This Month's New Titles</b>

22:53.560 --> 22:58.560
<b>Bookshop Prize
Recommendations!</b>

22:56.950 --> 22:58.560
I'm sorry.

22:58.560 --> 23:02.070
Actually, we've had another 
reverse-shoplifted book show up.

23:02.380 --> 23:05.230
It's an unusual one, 
so it's all yours, Ogawa-san.

23:05.230 --> 23:08.080
Oh, thank you.

23:08.080 --> 23:09.790
What book is it?

23:09.790 --> 23:11.510
If you want it, you can have it.

23:12.080 --> 23:13.960
<b>Ton</b>-chan the Glutton

23:13.960 --> 23:15.080
<b></b>I am happy

23:13.960 --> 23:15.080
<b>Try turning
the page</b>

23:15.080 --> 23:17.090
There's something written in it.

23:18.580 --> 23:22.580
<b></b>I am happy

23:18.580 --> 23:22.580
<b>Try turning
the page</b>

23:18.580 --> 23:22.590
"I am happy"?

23:23.330 --> 23:27.590
<b>Kitty Life</b>

23:24.050 --> 23:27.590
This means I get to play 
with him again, doesn't it?

23:27.590 --> 23:30.170
I wonder who wrote this.

23:31.600 --> 23:40.020
<b>A humble story
of friendship and parting.</b>

23:31.600 --> 23:40.020
<b>By Ogawa Sumireko,
author of <i>Simply Walk
Alone, Like a Rhino's Horn</i></b>

23:32.430 --> 23:38.980
